Third-party components

enzUI's own source, documentation, generated assets and screenshots are covered
by the MIT grant above. Six parts of this tree are third-party work,
redistributed under terms that grant does NOT override. Each entry names the
licence text this repository ships for it and the document recording where it
came from.

1. Lucide icon assets, `crates/enzui-icons`, declared `MIT AND ISC`. The
   bundled upstream Lucide SVGs are ISC and the Feather-derived subset is MIT;
   the framework code, the generated icon manifest and the fallback asset are
   MIT. Licence texts: `crates/enzui-icons/LICENSES/ISC.txt`,
   `crates/enzui-icons/LICENSES/MIT.txt` and
   `crates/enzui-icons/LICENSES/MIT-enzUI.txt`. Upstream commit and
   per-portion split: `crates/enzui-icons/THIRD_PARTY.md`. Redistributing
   the icon assets requires shipping those notices.

2. cryoglyph fork, `vendor/cryoglyph`, declared `MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR Zlib`, at
   the recipient's option. Licence texts: `vendor/cryoglyph/LICENSE-APACHE`,
   `vendor/cryoglyph/LICENSE-MIT` and `vendor/cryoglyph/LICENSE-ZLIB`. The
   committed tree is an altered version of upstream, which the Zlib option
   requires be plainly marked and the Apache option requires be stated:
   `vendor/cryoglyph/FORK.md` is that marking and names the upstream revision
   the patches are a diff against. Upstream's own MIT text carries no copyright
   line, so the holder is identified only through that provenance document.

3. zbus snapshot, `vendor/zbus`, declared `MIT`, copyright Zeeshan Ali Khan and
   zbus contributors. Licence text: `vendor/zbus/LICENSE`, the published
   crates.io archive's own file, unmodified. Archive identity and the one
   applied patch: `vendor/zbus/ENZUI_PATCH.md`.

4. Arsenal test font,
   `crates/enzui-widgets/tests/row_count_generation_font.ttf`, SIL Open
   Font License 1.1, copyright 2012 The Arsenal Project Authors. Licence text:
   `crates/enzui-widgets/tests/row_count_generation_font.OFL.txt`; the face
   is loaded by `crates/enzui-widgets/tests/font_load_runtime.rs`. The
   OFL forbids releasing the font under any other licence, so the MIT grant
   above does not reach it: redistribution must keep the copyright notice and
   the OFL text beside the file.

5. Bounded Curl media source, `vendor/gst-curl`, an altered MIT-licensed subset
   of GStreamer, copyright 2014 and 2017 British Broadcasting Corporation -
   Research and Development; author Sam Hurst. Licence text: `vendor/gst-curl/LICENSE-MIT`.
   Upstream commit, input hashes, alterations and carry/removal contract:
   `vendor/gst-curl/README.md` and `vendor/gst-curl/UPSTREAM.json`.

6. libarchive RAR test fixtures,
   `crates/enzui-services/tests/fixtures/archive/libarchive`, BSD-2-Clause,
   copyright Tim Kientzle and the libarchive contributors. Licence text:
   `crates/enzui-services/tests/fixtures/archive/libarchive/LICENSE`, libarchive's
   own `COPYING`. Source files and upstream names:
   `crates/enzui-services/tests/fixtures/archive/README.md`.

Outside this repository's source tree

`vendor/iced` is a working checkout of the enzICED fork of iced
(https://github.com/iced-rs/iced), which is MIT-licensed under its own
copyright. It is git-ignored here and is not part of this repository's source
tree; its licence travels with that checkout.

Dependencies resolved from crates.io are not redistributed in this tree. Each
one's licence is declared in its own package archive, which `Cargo.lock` pins by
SHA-256.
